Finally ascended on Sunday night; Possible (minor) spoilers, so you might
not want to read this...

First off, I was using a Valkyrie - this is definitely the character
class most likely to ascend. They start off hard to kill, have a
reasonable strength (>16) - no point in starting off with a high
strength since it is so easy to increase once you get going. They
usually have a fairly good dex too, although I don't usually pay much
attention to that - it'll stabilise at around 17, in my experience.
I do wish they were a bit more intelligent though - it would be nice to
be able to read spellbooks with impunity before you hit level 20....

Got a wish from a magic lamp early on - I *always* wish for a GDSM first
off. Taken with that +3 small shield, your armor class plummets and
you'll need one eventually anyway.

Got Mjollnir in the mine town and found GOP on a bones level. Mjollnir +
GOP is the most deadly combination in the game, beats Vorpy+GODex any
day, even when you have 18/** intrinsic strength. Got the luckstone from
the bottom level (I've heard people say it's hard to find! I don't get
this - it's always in the same place behind those secret doors on the
lowest mine level).

Went downwards in the Dungeons 'till I reached level 14, (No problem, I *love*
graveyards), did the quest. I think the Valkyrie quest is too easy. Sutur is a
doddle to kill, lots of giant corpses and gems so 18/** stength and intrinsic
fir res. and lots of points are guaranteed. The Orb is a pretty handy
item - warning, 1/2 spell damage and so on.

Minor hiccup when I paid a return visit to the temple in the mine town.
I accidentally threw an item at the priest and had to kill him. Bad
karma, but I was still piously alligned and I got back all the gold I'd
given him (around 50k). It didn't matter that much 'tho, I had an AC of
-32 for most of the game, and damn near everything missed me. I never did
get hit by a wand.

By that stage I had a bag of holding and a shitload of scrolls of
enchant weapon and enchant armor as well as around 20 potions of holy
water. Got Mjollnir up to +6, most of my armor to +4. Damn near
everything was blessed (and rustproof). Found a tinning kit as well (oh joy!).
I also had the good fortune to find a ring of levitation. Rings of
levitation are a must to get anywhere. Teleport control and conflict are
also real handy as well. If you don't find them, wish for them.
I generally go for a cloak of displacement rather than protection.
When you're invisible, displaced an have an AC of -32, you're pretty
hard to hit.

Went downwards, got another wish (Shield Of Reflection), killed Medusa
(blindfold+mirror). Arrived at the castle. Here's where Mjollnir really
comes into it's own. Used knock to drop the drawbridge, and a Giant
immediately threw a boulder at me. Oh joy! I stepped backwards, pushed
the boulder into the entranceway an started throwing Mjollnir over the
boulder. This is a great trick - the monsters can't get at you and
Mjollnir zaps them and returns to your hand as normal. Got all the
liches and rust monsters this way. Pushed the boulder in, cleaned up and
got my wand. Wished for Helm of telepathy (Invaluable in Hell), speed
boots, ring of conflict, AOLS, ring of teleport control. Kept one wish
handy which I used to replace an over-enchanted Shield of REflection
(stupid).

I cleaned out the rest of the castle (and indeed, the game) with
laughable ease. I cleaned out the  Barracks by leaving my finger on the
cursor keys for a while (2 seconds for each row of soldiers).

Went down to the valley, went up a few levels (those graveyards again).
I didn't use the Bell trick - things were easy enough as it was.
Went down through the levels of Hell (liked the abandoned town - those
shades are one of the nastiest things around, hard to kill and they
steal intrinsics). Killed Vlad (extra AOLS) and the Wizard, opened up
the entranceway to the last level. The wraiths in the graveyard got me
up to level 30. They'd been disturbed, but I just dispatched them safely
from a distance with Mjollnir (you might think that neutral characters
are disadvantaged because they have no artifact with the defend ability,
but Mjollnir makes up for this by allowing you to kill from a safe distance.)

I spent fucking *ages* trying to find the door to the temple. Thankfully
the book of the dead kindly kept me fed by periodically summoning up a bunch
of monsters (almost always at least one dragon). Indeed, it kept me fed for
most of the way back up as well, although the wizard summoning pets was
a help also (especially since they often killed the wizard for me).
When I did get in, I zorched the priest and the few nasties that didn't
kill each other (I said conflict was handy). Grabbed the amulet and started
back up. Halfway through hell, I copped the levitation trick and started
making very fast progress.

One thing: who the *FUCK* came up with Orcus? It kept on teleporting
next to me, almost always blocking my way and forcing me to wait a few
turns. It made progress throught the level that it was on very slow and very
frustrating.

Reached dlvl 1, picked up the pick-axe I had left behind and went to the
Earth level, found the portal very quickly and spent around twenty
minutes trying to find the air portal. The fire level took a while but
nowhere near as long as the air. At this point I disgusted some friends
by complaining that an Archon had hit me for 4 hit points damage!
(What's the big problem with these? Kill them while you're blind and
cure yourself with a unicorn horn).

The water level took a while - I got the approx location of the portal
from a detect gold scroll (it almost always seems to be on the other
side of the screen). A moster the kindly gave it's exact location
within the air bubble. A minor grouch - the air bubble should not alter
your position when you are levitating, but it does.

I didn't know you were supposed to remove your ring of conflict before
going to the astral plane, but ole Mjollnir polished off those angels
easily enough. I have to say that the astral plane was kinda easy. I
slaughtered everything in my path, (I was a bit dissapointed that I
couldn't tin Death or Pestilence :).

I didn't bother killing everything on the level - I found my temple
second try and ascended without further ado.

All in all, a pretty good game. Nice intrinsics, max apart from
intelligence and charisma. I never bothered with nurses, so I only had
346 HP, but I rarely went below 340 so it didn't matter much anyway.
I Got all the items (armor, rings, tools) I wanted, I didn't really need
any weapon apart from my +6 Mjollnir, but since I had received most of the
Neutral ones (except Vorpy) I kept a +4 Magicbane as a tin opener (no shit).
I had learned 20 or so spells, some of the quite useful (identify and magic
mapping particularly).

My bag of holding had 100,000$ and a shitload of gems I picked up. (No
polypiling). I stil had an AOLS and backup rings of conflict and
teleport control (someone said you need it to finish, this is not true).
Scored 5,182,856  pts. Not bad for a first ascension, eh?

	Gavin. (Happy (net)hacking!)

